WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.629
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.929 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:16.691
Unit twenty-two: Festivals Around the World. In this unit, you will talk about festivals in different countries.

4
00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:18.557
Festival.

5
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:22.858
Festival means a special time when people celebrate.

6
00:00:23.158 --> 00:00:25.344
Water Festival is in November.

7
00:00:26.044 --> 00:00:28.684
Your turn. Say: Festival.

8
00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:32.328
Festival.

9
00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:34.306
Lantern.

10
00:00:35.006 --> 00:00:38.608
Lantern means a light in a paper or glass box.

11
00:00:38.908 --> 00:00:40.954
We light lanterns at night.

12
00:00:41.654 --> 00:00:44.585
Your turn. Say: Lantern.

13
00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:48.100
Lantern.

14
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:50.106
Fireworks.

15
00:00:50.806 --> 00:00:54.048
Fireworks means colourful lights that explode in the sky.

16
00:00:54.348 --> 00:00:55.999
We watched the fireworks.

17
00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:59.456
Your turn. Say: Fireworks.

18
00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:03.157
Fireworks.

19
00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:04.872
Costume.

20
00:01:05.572 --> 00:01:08.826
Costume means special clothes for a festival or show.

21
00:01:09.126 --> 00:01:10.986
She wears a beautiful costume.

22
00:01:11.686 --> 00:01:14.327
Your turn. Say: Costume.

23
00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:17.923
Costume.

24
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:19.778
Dance.

25
00:01:20.478 --> 00:01:23.000
Dance means to move your body to music.

26
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.021
People dance in the street.

27
00:01:25.721 --> 00:01:28.467
Your turn. Say: Dance.

28
00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.110
Dance.

29
00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:34.048
Music.

30
00:01:34.748 --> 00:01:38.559
Music means nice sounds made by singing or instruments.

31
00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:40.812
The music is loud and happy.

32
00:01:41.512 --> 00:01:44.733
Your turn. Say: Music.

33
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:48.272
Music.

34
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:50.273
Celebrate.

35
00:01:50.973 --> 00:01:55.318
Celebrate means to do something special and fun for an event.

36
00:01:55.618 --> 00:01:57.733
We celebrate New Year in April.

37
00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:01.712
Your turn. Say: Celebrate.

38
00:02:04.412 --> 00:02:05.379
Celebrate.

39
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:07.233
Country.

40
00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:10.455
Country means a land with its own government.

41
00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:12.651
Every country has festivals.

42
00:02:13.351 --> 00:02:16.223
Your turn. Say: Country.

43
00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:19.704
Country.

44
00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:22.937
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:23.237 --> 00:02:25.527
Rithy, which festival do you like?

46
00:02:26.817 --> 00:02:30.351
I like Water Festival. People race boats on the river.

47
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.275
In China, people light lanterns at New Year.

48
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:39.697
In Brazil, people dance in costumes, right?

49
00:02:40.983 --> 00:02:46.503
Yes, at Carnival! And in America, people watch fireworks in July.

50
00:02:47.817 --> 00:02:50.014
Festivals are fun everywhere!

51
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:54.651
Grammar focus: People plus verb in (country).

52
00:02:54.951 --> 00:02:57.288
In China, people light lanterns.

53
00:02:57.588 --> 00:03:02.733
'People' is plural, so the verb has no -s: people dance, people light.

54
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.320
Now read and listen. Festivals Everywhere.

55
00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.339
People celebrate festivals in every country.

56
00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.472
In Cambodia, people race boats at Water Festival.

57
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:20.501
In China, people light red lanterns at New Year.

58
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:25.616
In Brazil, people wear costumes and dance to loud music.

59
00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:30.158
Festivals bring families and friends together.

60
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.311
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:34.611 --> 00:03:37.098
In China, people blank lanterns.

62
00:03:37.398 --> 00:03:40.855
A, light. B, lights. C, lighting.

63
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.128
The answer is A: light.

64
00:03:48.617 --> 00:03:50.686
Colourful lights in the sky are blank.

65
00:03:50.986 --> 00:03:56.334
A, fireworks. B, lanterns. C, costumes.

66
00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.918
The answer is A: fireworks.

67
00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:07.090
Special clothes for a festival are a blank.

68
00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.624
A, costume. B, music. C, country.

69
00:04:15.617 --> 00:04:18.034
The answer is A: costume.

70
00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:23.317
Now it's your turn to speak. Which festival would you like to see?

71
00:04:28.617 --> 00:04:33.661
I would like to see the lantern festival in China. People light hundreds of lanterns at night.

72
00:04:33.961 --> 00:04:35.577
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:42.208
Great work today! You learned eight new words and people plus verb in (country).

74
00:04:42.508 --> 00:04:47.192
Today's value is global friendship. Be a friend to children all around the world.

75
00:04:47.492 --> 00:04:51.735
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

76
00:04:52.035 --> 00:04:54.687
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

